          "recipeIngredient": [
            "1 1/2 Pounds Salmon (with the skin removed and cubed)",
            "1 Pinch Sea Salt",
            "2 Tablespoons Soy Sauce or Coconut Aminos",
            "2 Tablespoons Kewpie Mayo (or try my homemade mayo recipe!)",
            "1 1/2 Cups Cooked Sushi Rice",
            "1 Teaspoon Rice Vinegar",
            "12 Nori Squares",
            "1 Squeeze Kewpie Mayo",
            "1 Tablespoon Sesame Seeds",
            "1/4 Cup Green Onions (chopped)"
          ],
          "recipeInstructions": [
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "name": "Preheat oven",
              "text": "Start by preheating your oven to 400 F and lightly greasing a standard size muffin tin.",
              "url": "https://kalejunkie.com/viral-tiktok-baked-salmon-sushi-cups/#wprm-recipe-17764-step-0-0"
            },
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "name": "Prepare salmon",
              "text": "Next, add your cubed salmon, sea salt, soy sauce, and mayo to a large bowl. Toss to coat well, until all of the ingredients are fully combined.",
              "url": "https://kalejunkie.com/viral-tiktok-baked-salmon-sushi-cups/#wprm-recipe-17764-step-0-1"
            },
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "name": "Prepare rice",
              "text": "Then, add your cooked rice to a bowl and add in your vinegar. Mix until all of the rice is coated in the vinegar.",
              "url": "https://kalejunkie.com/viral-tiktok-baked-salmon-sushi-cups/#wprm-recipe-17764-step-0-2"
            },
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "name": "Prepare nori",
              "text": "Prepare your nori sheets by laying them out on a countertop. If using large nori sheets, cut them into squares small enough to fit into each cavity of your muffin tin.",
              "url": "https://kalejunkie.com/viral-tiktok-baked-salmon-sushi-cups/#wprm-recipe-17764-step-0-3"
            },
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "name": "Add Rice",
              "text": "Add about 2-3 tablespoons of your rice mixture to each nori sheet, then fold and place inside the muffin tin. Repeat until all of the cavities of your muffin tin are filled.",
              "url": "https://kalejunkie.com/viral-tiktok-baked-salmon-sushi-cups/#wprm-recipe-17764-step-0-4"
            },
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "name": "Top with Salmon",
              "text": "Then, top each nori cup with your salmon mixture. This will be about 2 tablespoons, depending on how big your salmon is!",
              "url": "https://kalejunkie.com/viral-tiktok-baked-salmon-sushi-cups/#wprm-recipe-17764-step-0-5"
            },
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "name": "Bake",
              "text": "Finally, bake your cups for 15 minutes, or until the salmon is cooked to your liking.",
              "url": "https://kalejunkie.com/viral-tiktok-baked-salmon-sushi-cups/#wprm-recipe-17764-step-0-6"
            },
            {
              "@type": "HowToStep",
              "name": "Garnish and enjoy",
              "text": "Once done, remove from the oven, top with your garnishes of choice, serve, and enjoy! These cups are best eaten the same day, but can be stored in an airtight container, in the fridge, for up to two days.",
              "url": "https://kalejunkie.com/viral-tiktok-baked-salmon-sushi-cups/#wprm-recipe-17764-step-0-7"
            }
          ],
